# ASP.NET Core Web API Deployment on IIS

## 1. Purpose

This document explains how to deploy an **ASP.NET Core Web API application** on **Microsoft IIS (Internet Information Services)**.

The deployment process consists of:

```text
Source Code
    ↓
Download / Clone Application
    ↓
Restore NuGet Packages
    ↓
Build Application
    ↓
Publish Application
    ↓
Install .NET Hosting Bundle
    ↓
Install / Configure IIS
    ↓
Create IIS Application Pool
    ↓
Create IIS Website/Application
    ↓
Configure SQL Server Permissions
    ↓
Test API
```

---

# 2. Prerequisites

Before starting, make sure the server/development machine has:

### Software

* Windows
* IIS
* .NET SDK required by the application
* ASP.NET Core Hosting Bundle
* SQL Server / SQL Express
* SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS)
* Git, if source code is stored in Git
* Web browser
* Administrator access

For our application:

```text
.NET: 8.0
Database: SQL Server Express
Database Name: Dapper
```

