# 32. Grant EXECUTE Permission on Stored Procedures

This is the **critical step that caused your HTTP 500 error**.

Your Event Viewer/IIS log showed:

```text
The EXECUTE permission was denied on the object 'sp_GetEmployee',
database 'Dapper', schema 'dbo'.
```

and:

```text
The EXECUTE permission was denied on the object 'sp_GetEmployeeById',
database 'Dapper', schema 'dbo'.
```

This means:

```text
IIS → Application → SQL Server
```

was actually working.

SQL Server recognized the IIS account.

But SQL Server was saying:

> "This account is allowed to connect to the database, but it is not allowed to execute this stored procedure."

