# 43. How to Diagnose IIS HTTP 500

When an IIS API gives:

```text
HTTP 500
```

do not immediately change IIS settings randomly.

Follow this sequence:

```text
Browser
   ↓
IIS
   ↓
ASP.NET Core
   ↓
Service
   ↓
Dapper
   ↓
SQL Server
```

Find the exact layer where the error occurs.

---

# 44. Check Application Logs

Your application was writing logs showing:

```text
Hosting environment: Production
Content root path: D:\IIS-Publish
```

Then:

```text
Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlException
```

This tells us:

### IIS is working

because the application started.

### ASP.NET Core is working

because the request reached the controller.

### Dapper is working

because Dapper attempted to execute SQL.

### SQL connection is working

because SQL Server returned a permission error.

### SQL permissions were the problem

because:

```text
EXECUTE permission was denied
```

This is an important diagnostic principle for future deployments.

